ints and took Black's lead from +14.5 to -1.2. The engine wanted E2. Opus 5.5's G3 on the previous turn had handed Black that big lead, and the 12k gave nearly all of it straight back."}, {"turn": 20, "text": "Opus 5.5 played F3, the game's worst move for either side at 16.3 points lost. It swung the lead from -1.2 to +15.1 for Black, and the engine's choice was F2. It repaid the 12k's gift in a single move."}, {"turn": 33, "text": "The 12k played F5 and lost 21.1 points, the biggest swing of the game. Black's lead went from +15.6 to -5.5, and the engine would have played J1. Black held a +15.6 lead before the move and was behind after it."}, {"turn": 35, "text": "J4 lost another 4.5 points and took Black's lead from -5.6 to -10.1. After F5, the 12k never found a way back, and White's lead kept growing."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "The only program run was libs.py, which parses a pasted board and prints each group's stones and liberties (no move generation or lookahead); the other commands just cat/tail and append to the notes files CLAUDE.md and games.md.", "stop": false}}